# This file is autogenerated from the template
*/.env
**/Dockerfile
# ...except under Examples/, where the Dockerfiles are hand-written parts of a
# quick start rather than gomplate output from a Dockerfile.tpl. Without this
# negation a fresh clone (or a git worktree) cannot run the documented
# `docker compose up --build` in Examples/snmp-simulator: the file is simply
# absent and the build fails with "failed to read dockerfile".
# Nothing under Examples/ is generated by Scripts/Install/configure.sh; a test in
# Common/Tests/Server/Infrastructure/ExampleDockerfiles.test.ts fails if a
# Dockerfile.tpl is ever added there, which is when this would need narrowing.
!Examples/**/Dockerfile
config.env
config.env.tmp
config.env.temp
logs.txt

